#====================================================================
# Draft knowledge entry - self-hosting language toolchain on OHOS:
#   prebuilt bootstrap binary lacks .codesign (EACCES), monolithic
#   libLLVM must override llvm-config component list, gnu-targeted
#   bootstrap needs glibc-symbol shims
# Source package: crystal/1.21.1
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-ohos-crystal-1.21.1-prebuilt-bootstrap-sign-and-monolithic-llvm
trigger_tool:           crystal|shards|make|clang|lld|binary-sign-tool|llvm-config
phase:                  source|build|link|test

error_signature:        sh: .*crystal: Permission denied|Permission denied.*crystal|unable to find library -lLLVM[A-Za-z]+|unable to find library -lLLVMRISCVDisassembler|undefined symbol: __xpg_strerror_r|undefined symbol: pthread_setcancelstate|can't find file 'c/fcntl'|can't find file 'markd'|error executing command: id -[ug]n, got exit status 1|libgc could not be found

severity:               3
category:               toolchain|self-hosting|elf-signing|llvm|compat-shim|environment
match_keywords:         OHOS, crystal, crystal-lang, self-hosting, bootstrap, prebuilt binary, codesign, EACCES, Permission denied, monolithic libLLVM, LLVM_LDFLAGS, llvm-config, musl target, __xpg_strerror_r, pthread_setcancelstate, shards, CRYSTAL_PATH, lib_c, id -gn, id -un
title:                  Self-hosting toolchains on OHOS: sign the prebuilt bootstrap, override the LLVM component list, and shim glibc-only symbols

root_cause:             A self-hosting language ships a prebuilt bootstrap compiler that must
                        RUN on OHOS before it can build the new compiler, and three
                        independent obstacles stack up.  (1) The official release binary has
                        no .codesign section, so execve returns EACCES even though mode bits,
                        uid/gid, SELinux context and hmdfs permission attributes are identical
                        to a locally built binary that runs fine.  (2) The build links LLVM via
                        `llvm-config --libs`, which lists 110 component libraries
                        (libLLVMX86CodeGen, libLLVMRISCVDisassembler, ...), while the OHOS SDK
                        ships only three monolithic libLLVM files (libLLVM.so, libLLVM-15.so,
                        libLLVM-15.0.4.so); --link-shared does not help because it looks for
                        libLLVMSupport.so and friends, which are equally absent.  (3) The
                        official bootstrap is built for the gnu target, and its stdlib picks
                        lib_c bindings by the target it was BUILT for - not by the --target
                        passed to new compilations - so generated code references glibc-only
                        names (__xpg_strerror_r from lib_c/aarch64-linux-gnu/c/string.cr:8,
                        pthread_setcancelstate from crystal/system/unix/process.cr:262,267)
                        that musl does not provide.

affected_scope:         Self-hosting language toolchains on OHOS that (a) ship a prebuilt
                        bootstrap binary, (b) link LLVM through llvm-config, or (c) came from a
                        gnu-targeted build.  Measured end to end on crystal 1.21.1: 1625 .cr
                        files and 0 .c/.h files; the compiler builds to a 47 MB aarch64 binary
                        and runs after signing (reports Crystal 1.21.1), and it compiles a
                        runnable OHOS binary with --target aarch64-unknown-linux-musl.

verification_cmd:       llvm-readelf -S ./bin/crystal | grep -c codesign ; ./bin/crystal --version

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           sign-bootstrap-then-override-llvm-then-shim
rec_description:        Four ordered steps, each independently measured.
                        (1) SIGN: binary-sign-tool sign -inFile <bootstrap>/bin/crystal
                        -outFile <signed> -selfSign 1, chmod 755.  Sign bin/shards as well -
                        it has the same missing section and fails the same way.
                        (2) OVERRIDE LLVM: point LLVM_CONFIG at a wrapper script that is
                        itself *named* llvm-config and placed first on PATH; the wrapper
                        answers --libs / --ldflags / --system-libs with the monolithic
                        library (-lLLVM-15.0.4) and forwards every other subcommand to the
                        real llvm-config.  Measured: merely exporting LLVM_LDFLAGS does NOT
                        work - crystal still runs `llvm-config --libs`, gets the 110
                        component library names the SDK does not ship, and the link dies
                        with "unable to find library -lLLVMX86CodeGen".  The wrapper name
                        and its PATH position are what matter (crystal's
                        find-llvm-config.sh resolves `llvm-config` through PATH).
                        (3) SHIM glibc names: forward __xpg_strerror_r to musl's strerror_r (same
                        XSI signature); return-0 stubs for pthread_setcancelstate /
                        pthread_setcanceltype (justified: the runtime libc exports them as weak
                        symbols, so "missing at link time" != "absent at run time").
                        (4) POINT CRYSTAL_PATH correctly: it must include lib (for shards such
                        as markd), src, and src/lib_c/<triple> (for `require "c/fcntl"`).
rec_command:            PATH=<wrapper-dir>:$PATH LLVM_CONFIG=<wrapper-dir>/llvm-config make
                        --jobserver-style=pipe -j4 crystal CRYSTAL=<signed>
                        FLAGS="--target aarch64-unknown-linux-musl" LDFLAGS="-L<libgc>/lib <shim>.o"
                        # <wrapper-dir>/llvm-config = compat/llvm-config-ohos, copied under
                        # the name llvm-config so crystal's PATH lookup finds it.
                        # Do NOT rely on LLVM_LDFLAGS alone: measured ineffective.
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               recipe-source-layout

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      static-deps-to-avoid-abi-mixing
fallback_description:   --target aarch64-unknown-linux-musl and OHOS-built shared objects pull
                        in conflicting ABIs: linking an ohos .so reports "libxxx.so is
                        incompatible with aarch64linux".  Prefer static dependencies where
                        available (numactl/libgc/libpcre2 are static-only on ohpcd already) or
                        keep every dependency on one ABI.
fallback_command:       crystal build prog.cr --target aarch64-unknown-linux-musl --link-flags="-L<libgc>/lib"
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          build-option

forbid_1_pattern:       foreign aarch64 binary.*(incompatible|not supported).*(so|wontfix)|conclude glibc-vs-musl incompatibility from Permission denied
forbid_1_reason:        Falsified by measurement: a locally built FULLY STATIC binary (e_type=EXEC,
                        no INTERP, no NEEDED), padded to ~130 MB and placed in the same
                        directory, runs fine.  The only decisive difference is that the local
                        binary has a .codesign section and the released one has none.
forbid_1_consequence:   Wrongly writing off an adaptable package as unsupported, while the
                        actual remedy is one signing command.

forbid_2_pattern:       link using plain llvm-config --libs output on OHOS|assume LLVM_LDFLAGS fixes the component-library list
forbid_2_reason:        It names 110 component libraries that the OHOS SDK does not ship
                        (only a monolithic libLLVM exists), and exporting LLVM_LDFLAGS does
                        not change that list - measured: the build still links the 110 names.
                        The working remedy is LLVM_CONFIG pointing at a wrapper that is named
                        llvm-config and sits first on PATH.
forbid_2_consequence:   Immediate link failure with dozens of "unable to find library -lLLVM..."
                        lines; no amount of -L tweaking or LLVM_LDFLAGS helps.

forbid_3_pattern:       delete the id -[ug]n spec|remove GROUP_NAME spec|patch group_spec to skip
forbid_3_reason:        The failure is a host accounting quirk (uid/gid without a name mapping),
                        not a defect in the test or the package.  A runner-level PATH shim that
                        falls back to the numeric id preserves the assertion.
forbid_3_consequence:   Silently losing user/group spec coverage.

forbid_4_pattern:       sign only crystal but not shards|single sign step is enough
forbid_4_reason:        Both binaries in the release archive lack .codesign and both are
                        executed during the build.
forbid_4_consequence:   The build gets past the compiler but dies when shards is invoked.

similar_to:             [DRAFT-E077B-ohos-sdk-autocodesign-invalid, DRAFT-332-openrct2-0.5.3-libcpp15-cpp20-compat, DRAFT-eigen-3.4.1-make-jobserver-mkfifo-nonfatal, DRAFT-aml-1.0.0-ohos-pthread-setcancelstate-meson-feature-detect]
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

notes_codesign_signal:  Distinguishing this from E077B is the first diagnostic:
                        `llvm-readelf -S <bin> | grep -c codesign` returns 0 here (no section at
                        all) versus 1 for the SDK-autocodesign case.  E077B: fake signature
                        present, remove then re-sign.  This entry: no signature, just sign.
notes_shards_sign:      bin/shards in the release archive is unsigned too and fails identically;
                        it must be signed before `shards install`.
notes_crystal_path:     Omitting lib/ yields "can't find file 'markd'"; omitting
                        src/lib_c/<triple> yields "can't find file 'c/fcntl'".  Both error
                        messages misleadingly suggest running `shards install`, so the real
                        cause (a missing CRYSTAL_PATH component) is easy to miss.
notes_jobserver:        The make "jobserver mkfifo: Operation not permitted" warning appears
                        here as well and is likewise NON-FATAL, matching
                        DRAFT-eigen-3.4.1-make-jobserver-mkfifo-nonfatal.
notes_openssl_version: A FIFTH gate, and the one that unblocks everything else: crystal
                        binds OpenSSL 1.1 macro names (sk_value, sk_pop_free,
                        EVP_CIPHER_flags) whenever it decides the OpenSSL version is
                        unknown.  It decides that with a compile-time macro running
                        `pkg-config --modversion libcrypto`, which silently yields
                        "0.0.0" when PKG_CONFIG_PATH is unset, selecting the 1.1 bare-name
                        branch in src/openssl/lib_crypto.cr.  Do NOT chase these symbols
                        one by one - export PKG_CONFIG_PATH pointing at each dependency's
                        lib/pkgconfig and the entire sk_*/EVP_* error chain disappears at
                        once (verified: pkg-config then reports 3.5.8, and the spec suite
                        compiles).
notes_remaining:        Closed out.  The 67 failures / 38 errors are attributed by category
                        (chmod and readlink under hmdfs which ignores chmod, user/group with
                        no name mapping, tempfile, XML, exception-memory) in the recipe's
                        notes.md and test_package/MANIFEST.yml; the conanfile recipe was
                        produced and local conan create validation PASSED (CREATE_RC=0);
                        the PR was opened.  Six gates are recorded above so the work need
                        not be rediscovered.
notes_status:           Measured: compiler MAKE_RC=0 (47 MB aarch64), runs as "Crystal 1.21.1
                        (2026-09-26)", compiles a runnable hello-world for
                        aarch64-unknown-linux-musl, and the upstream spec suite builds and
                        runs: 18066 examples, 67 failures, 38 errors, 32 pending, i.e.
                        17929 passing, in 4:29.
